      "heading": "Overview",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Use the `div()` function in the expression of a matchmaking rule to divide two numbers.",
          "refs": []
        }
      ],
      "listItems": []
    },
    {
      "level": 3,
      "heading": "Declaration",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "```other\nnumber div(number $dividend, number $divisor)\n```",
          "refs": []
        }
      ],
      "listItems": []
    },
    {
      "level": 3,
      "heading": "Parameters",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "-`dividend`: The number that the function divides. -`divisor`: The number that the function divides into `dividend`.",
          "refs": []
        }
      ],
      "listItems": []
    },
    {
      "level": 3,
      "heading": "Return value",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "The result or quotient of dividing `divisor` into `dividend`. If `divisor` is `zero`, `null`.",
          "refs": []
        }
      ],
